  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: NW part of upper Euphrates basin. According to Wikipedia, possibly Gaziantep (Turkey).</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Antiocheia pros Tauro or Antiochia ad Taurum was a Hellenistic city located in Cilicia. Some modern scholarship places the ancient city at the site of modern Gaziantep, Gaziantep Province, Turkey.",
